===Etymology 2===
Possibly from a lost {{m|la|*dex}} (seen in {{m|la|index}} > {{m|la|indicō}}, {{m|la|iūdex}} > {{m|la|iūdicō}}, {{m|la|vindex}} > {{m|la|vindicō}}), from {{der|la|ine-pro|*deyḱ-s}}, root nomen agentis from {{m|ine-pro|*deyḱ-||to show}}, whence {{m|la|dīcō}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{la-IPA|dicō}}
* {{audio|la-cls-dico.ogg|Audio (Classical)|lang=la}}

====Verb====
{{la-verb|dicō|dicāre|dicāvī|dicātum|conj=1}}

# I [[dedicate]], [[devote]].
# I [[consecrate]], [[deify]].
# I [[appropriate]] to, [[devote]] to, [[assign]] to, [[set apart]] for.

